Templates in C++ allow you to write **generic code** that can work with **any data type**. This is a powerful feature that enables **generic programming**, which is not possible in C.

**Why is it useful?**  
You can write a single function or class that works with `int`, `float`, `string`, or any user-defined type, without writing separate code for each type.

